packages.description:
keys.ts: deterministic secp256k1 and P-256 test keys (fixed scalars, test-only) and their did:key multikeys.

signed-repo.ts: `SignedRepo(did, key)` builds a real MST with @atcute/mst (NodeWrangler / MST APIs) and @atcute/cbor, and signs v3 commits with @atcute/crypto. It supports:
- `put`, `delete` and `commit()`, which return `{cid, rev, blocks}`;
- `getRecordCar(collection, rkey)` for inclusion or exclusion proofs;
- `getBlocks(cids)`;
- `fullCar()`;
- corruption helpers that each alter exactly one invariant: signature, block byte, MST node, DID, version, rev, root, truncate, oversize, record-CID swap.

fake-pds.ts: an XRPC handler (a Request→Response function) per PDS host. It serves:
- getRecord, getBlocks, getRepo, getLatestCommit, getRepoStatus and listRecords;
- createRecord, putRecord and deleteRecord with swapRecord semantics and RecordAlreadyExists / InvalidSwap errors. Authentication is a fixture bearer token; DPoP is not validated.

Fault injection: deactivate/takedown, key rotation, 429 with Retry-After, 5xx, redirects, oversize, a stale head (serving an older commit), `getBlocks` unsupported (501), BlockNotFound after GC, and no-proof RecordNotFound.

Every call is logged so tests can count remote calls.

Other fakes:
- fake-plc.ts: a DID document per DID, with rotation.
- fake-doh.ts: dns-json answers, with public test-net addresses by default and private-answer injection.
- fake-relay.ts: listReposByCollection paging.
- fake-jetstream.ts: an event log with seq, cursor-inclusive replay, a lookback bound, and a WebSocketPair driver that the test controls (send, close, error).

router-transport.ts: `routerTransport({pds:{host→fake}, plc, doh, relay})` is a Transport marked `fixture:true`.

read-models.ts: `seedReadModels(kit)` publishes tests/fixtures/read_models.json exactly:
- Alice, Bob and Carol on separate fake PDS hosts;
- r08 created then deleted;
- the Alice→Bob follow;
- Carol's r10 as an external writer.

It returns a map from URI to `{cid, rev}` and the Jetstream events. CIDs and revisions are produced by the signer and never fabricated.

scripts/gen-config.ts reads PUBLIC_ORIGIN, LEXICON_PREFIX and the env name (production, staging or local). It writes:
- web/public/oauth/client-metadata.json: client_id equal to its own URL; client_name; client_uri; `redirect_uris [origin+'/oauth/callback']`; `scope 'atproto repo:<p>.scrobble repo:<p>.follow repo:<p>.settings'`; `grant_types [authorization_code, refresh_token]`; `response_types [code]`; `application_type web`; `token_endpoint_auth_method none`; `dpop_bound_access_tokens true`.
- web/public/_headers: the CSP and the other headers from ADR §8.

For local env it emits only a loopback client-id hint file for the SPA, not metadata. It refuses to write production metadata when LEXICON_PREFIX is empty or the fixture prefix.

scripts/check-bundle.ts runs `wrangler deploy --dry-run --outdir worker/dist`, then asserts:
- the gzip size is ≤ 3 MiB;
- there are no `test-support`, `fixedClock`, `routerTransport` or `node:crypto` strings or imports;
- there is no `secp256k1-node` module;
- the bundle SHA-256 is printed for release evidence.

All functions are synchronous over a Db and are called inside `db.tx`.

`applyRecordProof(db, proof: RecordProof, {receiptNs, prefix, nowNs})` returns `{outcome: 'applied'|'noop_older'|'excluded'|'absent'|'stale_head'}`. It enforces:
- the per-DID floor: `proof.commit.rev < users.max_rev` gives stale_head;
- the per-URI guard: `record_state.revision ≥ rev` gives noop.

For `scrobble`:
- validate with W1-01;
- compute keys with W1-02 (keys.ts maps them to columns);
- upsert the scrobbles row with revision = commit.rev;
- set record_state to present;
- on an invalid record, delete the row and set excluded with the reason;
- on absent, delete the row and set absent;
- bump `users.stats_version` when a scrobble row changed;
- update `max_rev`.

`follow` follows the same pattern. `settings` delegates to suppression.ts.

`applySnapshotChunk(db, {did, generation, headRev, intervalLo, intervalHi, entries: Array<{key, cid, record?: unknown}>, receiptNs})`:
- upserts the present entries that have record bodies, skipping those whose CID equals the stored CID;
- deletes rows of the DID whose URI lies in `(at://did/lo, at://did/hi]`, whose key is absent from entries, and whose revision < headRev;
- writes the record_state transitions.

`completeSnapshot(db, {did, generation, headRev, accountActive})`: if `users.generation == generation` and the DID is not suppressed, set active per accountActive, `indexing_state='current'` and `last_snapshot_at_ms`. Otherwise it is a no-op returning `superseded`.

account-state.ts:
- `markInactive(db, did, status)` sets active=0 and increments generation (ADR 0003 generation semantics).
- `markReactivating(db, did)` keeps the account hidden and sets `reactivate=1` on the snapshot job.

suppression.ts: `applySettings(db, did, proof)`. Disabled leads to `disconnectLocalData` (deletes per ADR §5.3, inserts suppression with settings_uri and settings_rev). Enabled, or an absent record with a higher revision, deletes suppression and returns `admit:true`.

read/visibility.ts exports SQL fragments for active, unsuppressed users, used by all readers.

Indexing high-water marks (W2-05 amendment): every write that stamps `indexed_at` (the projection rows applied by applyRecordProof and applySnapshotChunk, and the users row in completeSnapshot and the per-apply user advance) calls `noteIndexed(db, did, nowNs)` from worker/src/do/status.ts in the same tx instead of setting `users.indexed_at` itself, so `indexing()` reports the global lastIndexedAt (`indexing_status('global').last_indexed_at`) as well as the per-user one. These modules never set `indexing_status` values (deleting the DID's own scope row on disconnect is allowed). The W2-05 source guard in worker/test/storage/status.test.ts fails otherwise.

hints.ts:
- `enqueueHints(db, hints[], checkpoint?)` is a synchronous coalescing upsert. It optionally advances `ingest_checkpoint` in the same tx.
- `takeDue(db, now, n, priority order)`.
- backoff and delete helpers.
- `countByDid` for coalescing.

admission.ts:
- `admit(db, did, source, now)` enforces the hourly budget (default 50) and the 1,024 pending-snapshot cap.
- On admission, insert `users(active=0)` and `repo_jobs(snapshot)` with a new global generation, atomically.
- Return `{admitted}` or `{busy}`, with nothing written when busy.
- Also `scheduleSnapshot(db, did, reason)`, used by sweeps and coalescing.

verify-drain.ts: `drain(m, now, budget)` implements ADR §5.4 exactly.
- suppressed handling;
- admission for unknown DIDs;
- coalescing at ≥25 hints for one DID;
- identity via identity-cache.ts (identity_cache table; TTL 5 min, negative 1 h);
- skip a host while `host_backoff` is set;
- fetch getRecord through SafeFetch;
- the verified_commits cache;
- verifyRecordProof;
- one db.tx calling applyRecordProof, then delete the hint.

Error mapping: no_proof, missing_block or an unparseable CAR schedules a snapshot; RepoDeactivated and similar errors create a status job; bad_signature gets one fresh-resolve retry and then fails closed; transient errors back off; give up after 20 attempts and schedule a snapshot.

Concurrency: at most 4 concurrent fetches and 2 per host. An in-flight URI set prevents double fetch. No db.tx may span an await.

pds-budget.ts: per-host concurrency and backoff from Retry-After / RateLimit-Reset.

The PLAN=free budget is 40 subrequests.

Checkpoint advance (W2-05 amendment): the optional checkpoint advance of `enqueueHints` calls `recordEvent(db, {cursor, timeUs})` from worker/src/do/status.ts in the same tx. hints.ts holds no SQL that writes ingest_checkpoint (the W2-05 source guard fails otherwise), so an event can never move the stale reference instant.

POST /api/v1/notify:
- body ≤ 2 KiB (413);
- strict JSON `{uri}` or `{did}`; unknown fields 422;
- AT-URI with a configured collection, or a valid DID;
- the Worker forwards clientIp.

DO `notify(m, input, ip, now)`:
- applies the per-IP bucket (60/min) and per-DID bucket (600/h), giving 429 with Retry-After;
- a suppressed DID is accepted only for the settings collection, and silently ignored with 202 otherwise;
- `{uri}` enqueues a hint with source notify at top priority;
- `{did}` admits the DID if unknown, or schedules a refresh snapshot if the last snapshot was more than 24 h ago (at most once per 24 h);
- busy gives 503 queue_full;
- success gives 202 `{state:'queued'}`.

GET /api/v1/records/status?uri= returns `{uri, state, cid?, revision?, reason?, indexing}`:
- indexed: a visible row;
- pending: a hint or job exists;
- absent or excluded: from record_state;
- unknown otherwise.

It is `no-store`.

worker/src/do/index-do.ts: `class IndexDO extends DurableObject implements IndexRpc`.
- **Constructor:** runs `blockConcurrencyWhile(migrate)`, `deps = this.buildDeps(env, ctx)` (protected; production uses systemClock, cryptoRandom, fetch, the identity resolver and connectJetstream), marks connected=false through W2-05 `markDisconnected` (which writes only on the 1→0 transition, so a restart never moves the disconnect instant), and ensures the timers and alarm.
- **`alarm()`:** calls `runDue` with handlers drain → verify-drain, snapshot → snapshotStep, jetstream-watchdog → socket or pulse, status-sweep, identity-sweep, discovery, and gc (prunes snapshot_blocks of finished jobs, verified_commits older than 7 d, stale identity_cache entries and old hint errors), then `armAlarm`.
- **RPC methods** wrap the module functions and match IndexRpc. `ensureRunning` re-arms the alarm.
- **`adminPitr(atMs)`:** `getBookmarkForTime`, then `onNextSessionRestoreBookmark`, then `ctx.abort()`.

worker/src/router.ts concatenates the `routes` exports of every worker/src/http/*.ts module. An unknown /api/* path gets a JSON 404 envelope.

worker/src/index.ts `fetch`:
- strips inbound `x-atmusic-*` headers;
- sets clientIp from CF-Connecting-IP and a requestId;
- imports the cursor key once per isolate;
- gets the stub with `env.INDEX.get(env.INDEX.idFromName('index-v1'), {locationHint})`;
- dispatches through the router;
- serves `/health/live` locally;
- passes anything else to ASSETS.

scheduled.ts: `ensureRunning()`, plus starting a pulse in pulse mode.

http/admin.ts: /internal/admin/status, /internal/admin/pitr and /internal/admin/resnapshot, enabled only when ADMIN_TOKEN is set, with a constant-time bearer compare. Missing token or disabled gives 404.

The production entry never imports test-support, and `scripts/check-bundle.ts` must pass.

scripts/e2e/dev-env.ts starts @atproto/dev-env (a local PDS and PLC; test-only Node infrastructure) with two accounts on separate PDS instances where supported.

worker/test/e2e/entry.ts: an IndexDO subclass whose transport allows http loopback for the dev-env hosts only, with INGEST_MODE=off. Ingestion comes through notify and snapshots, and the fixture prefix is allowed.

start-stack.ts runs gen-config (local), vite build and `wrangler dev --config worker/test/e2e/wrangler.e2e.jsonc --ip 127.0.0.1 --port 8787`.

The journey:
1. sign in with the loopback client;
2. submit a scrobble and see it indexed;
3. browse the feed, profile, history and stats windows;
4. follow and unfollow the second account;
5. delete the scrobble and see it absent;
6. export;
7. disconnect, then reconnect;
8. sign out.

accessibility.spec.ts runs axe on every route.

.github/workflows/deploy.yml: manual dispatch, run in an environment-protected job using CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN. Steps:
1. `npm ci`;
2. `bash scripts/check-ts.sh`;
3. gen-config (production);
4. `vite build`;
5. `wrangler versions upload`, recording the version id and the bundle SHA-256 from check-bundle;
6. `wrangler versions deploy <id>@100%`;
7. a smoke test of /health/live, /health/ready and /api/v1/meta.

scripts/deploy.sh does the same locally and refuses when LEXICON_PREFIX is empty or the fixture prefix, or the CURSOR_KEY secret is missing (checked with `wrangler secret list`).

scripts/admin/pitr-restore.ts calls /internal/admin/pitr.

